		{"id":"fix","type":"text","text":"**Return-value observability fix**\nLogic-bug detection: 91.18% → 100% (same-lineage); 77.94% → 88.24% (cross-implementation).\nCross-implementation false alarms 25% → 10% under `task_only` (sensitivity cost stated openly).","x":400,"y":200,"width":380,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e2e","type":"text","text":"**E2E harness built on this module's methodology (PR #77)**\n`demo/eval_e2e/` — mutation operators + Clopper-Pearson CIs ported to the full M01→M02→M03 chain: abstention 0.462 (n=26), detection 0.357 (n=14), false-alarm 0.000 (n=2), cx quality 0.800 (n=5).","x":800,"y":280,"width":360,"height":190,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"audit","type":"text","text":"**Evidence trail**\nMeasured results committed in `eval/results/*.md`; archived pre-fix reports kept as an audit trail; re-verified byte-identical in Session B's combined re-run.","x":0,"y":400,"width":360,"height":140,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"v2weak","type":"text","text":"**V2 symbolic ≈ no contribution**\nContainer-shaped inputs force V1 fallback on the current corpus — the 'multi-modal' certificate is effectively V1-driven. Now stated in the prominent docs (PR #83), not just the eval reports.","x":400,"y":420,"width":380,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"eqmut","type":"text","text":"**Equivalent-mutant specificity**\nOnly 0.1111.","x":800,"y":510,"width":340,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"numeric","type":"text","text":"**Numeric-boundary blind spot**\n`<` vs `<=` at a threshold (e.g. `credit_score=600`): V1 samples ints uniformly from −100..100 and V2 is not a per-input oracle.","x":0,"y":580,"width":400,"height":150,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gil","type":"text","text":"**Timeout limit**\nThread-based B3 timeout bounds GIL-releasing hangs only; a GIL-monopolizing C-level statement is not preemptible without process isolation — the named honest leftover.","x":460,"y":610,"width":360,"height":150,"color":"2"}
